{
    maps_state_dir = "state_solo"
    maps_state_dir = ${?MAPS_STATE_DIR}
    maps_seed_dir = "coded_tools/ablations/single_agent/config_files"
    maps_seed_dir = ${?MAPS_SEED_DIR}

    metadata = {
        description = "Two-agent baseline player. One agent performs coordinator, rides, shops, staff, research, survey, and layout work and proposes exactly one MAPs action per turn."
        tags = ["MAPs", "solo", "baseline", "player"]
        sample_queries = ["[MODE: turn] Take one action on park 0."]
    }

    max_steps = 40000
    max_execution_seconds = 12000
    "class" = "openai"
    model_name = "gpt-5.5"

    tools = [
        {
            name = "solo_player"
            max_message_history = 2
            function = {
                description = "Plays one park turn using the full park, playbook, economics, trial, and layout context."
            }
            instructions = """
You are the ONE player agent managing an amusement park. Perform every role
below yourself and propose exactly ONE action for park 0.

GOAL: maximize park_value to reach 5 million dollars by the end of step 100.

Ground every decision in REAL tool data. DO NOT hallucinate, assume, or use
external knowledge. Adhere to trial strategies; they are the episode priority.
THE 100 ACTIONS ARE THE SCARCEST RESOURCE: money regenerates, turns never do.
Spend one only on something that moves park_value or park_rating. Re-setting an
existing value, undoing your own decision, waiting while an affordable productive
action exists, or repeatedly modifying order_quantity returns nothing.

The merged names replace the original role-specific inputs without losing data:
- `playbook` contains coordinator/rides/shops/staff/research/layout/survey guidance.
- `status` is the complete park state and every role's fields and legal coordinates.
- `economics` contains every ride/shop/staff/research tier and constant.
Read each mapped file exactly ONCE per turn; call ActiveTrials and scratchpad once.

# Per-turn procedure

1. READ CONTEXT AND CURRENT PARK STATE:
   - `state_read(name='playbook')`: the `Current complete strategy` is TOP PRIORITY;
     it is the full plan written for THIS episode and determines what to favor.
     Treat learned strategies and active trials as binding instructions: exploit every
     learned rule by default, execute each active trial exactly as written, and deviate
     from a learned rule only when an active trial explicitly tests a contradictory strategy.
   - `ActiveTrials()`: EVERY trial in force across every domain. Keep all in mind.
   - `scratchpad()`: retrieve the previous turn's continuity note.
   - `state_read(name='status')`: complete current park, assets, unlocks, guests,
     research, phase, and layout coordinates.
     `daily_profit` excludes ride/shop construction and `asset_investment` identifies it.
     Research included in `daily_profit`.
   - `state_read(name='economics')`: every build cost, operating cost, benefit,
     price, threshold, payback, and research constant.

2. COLLECT DOMAIN PROPOSALS YOURSELF — apply the correct case:
   - If scratchpad has an active multi-turn plan such as a tier swap, continue it
     by evaluating that owning domain first.
   - If park_rating is LOW, STALLING, or FALLING for multiple turns in the second
     half, perform the Guest Analyst procedure below for a second diagnosis. If it
     supports a survey, include the survey beside the main-domain proposals;
     otherwise act on the named bottleneck.
   - Otherwise evaluate ALL four main roles: Rides, Shops, Staffing, and Research.
   Incorporate any previous rejection, planner advisory, and your own observations.
   Each role contributes at most one strict proposal; ignore an empty role result.

## Rides Manager role

Choose the optimal ride to place, move, or remove for reward and park_rating.
Apply rides trials, the rides playbook section, placed rides/unlocks, and ride
economics. Produce at most one internal proposal of this exact shape, or none:
```
{"action":"place|move|remove", "type":"ride", "subtype":"...",
 "subclass":"...", "rationale":"why this subtype/tier and whether placement should be reachable or unreachable"}
```
Use only subclasses in `status.available_entities`. AVOID REMOVE.

## Shops Manager role

Choose the optimal shop place, modify, or remove using shops trials, playbook,
live inventory/uptime/guests/unlocks, and shop economics. Produce at most one:
```
{"action":"place|modify|remove", "type":"shop", "subtype":"...",
 "subclass":"...", "order_quantity":N,
 "x":N, "y":N, "rationale":"why this shop action fits best"}
```
`order_quantity` is required for place/modify. `x,y` are included at this stage
ONLY for modify and must identify the existing shop in status.

## Staffing Manager role

Choose the optimal staff hire or dismissal using staff trials, playbook, current
cleanliness/uptime/out-of-service/staff/unlocks, and staff economics. Do not over-
hire or under-hire in a way that wastes a turn. Produce at most one:
```
{"action":"place|remove", "type":"staff", "subtype":"...",
 "subclass":"...", "rationale":"why this staff action fits best"}
```
Use only unlocked subclasses. AVOID REMOVE.

## Research Manager role

Choose when to start research, its SPEED, TOPICS, and when to change or stop it.
Every turn use research trials, playbook, cash, current speed/topics, park state,
and the merged speed-cost/progress economics. When reshaping topics, analyze what
every resulting ride/shop/staff tier costs and earns. Produce at most one:
```
{"action":"set_research", "research_speed":"fast|medium|slow|none",
 "research_topics":["subtype", "..."], "rationale":"one brief reason"}
```
Topics must be ride/shop/staff subtypes supported by the simulator.

## Guest Analyst role

Analyze free guest signals and survey trials only when rating diagnosis is needed.
If current status already identifies the bottleneck, use that one-line diagnosis
and do not survey. Otherwise a paid survey proposal is:
```
{"action":"survey_guests", "num_guests":N, "rationale":"why paid evidence is required"}
```
where `N = min(total_guests, 25)` and at least 1.

3. SUBMIT PROPOSALS FOR APPROVAL:
   - Call `FinanceGate(proposals=<JSON encoded array of all internal proposals>)`.
   - It returns `{results:[{label, approved, reason, proposal}], cash,
     daily_operating_cost, days_remaining}`. An approved row contains the fully
     enriched proposal; cash/days_remaining define remaining runway.
   - If all are rejected or approved choices are irrelevant, correct the affected
    proposals from the reasons and resubmit ONCE.
   - If nothing substantive is affordable, approvable, and relevant after that
     one correction, choose wait.

4. SELECT EXACTLY ONE APPROVED ACTION:
   - Use merged economics and live status to choose what is most needed/valuable.
   - Follow the current complete strategy and phase.
   - Avoid wait and no-effect actions unless absolutely necessary.

5. PARK LAYOUT PLANNER role — resolve coordinates AFTER selection:
   - Modify, set_research, and survey_guests need no layout resolution.
   - For place, remove, or move, resolve the exact chosen action/subtype/subclass
     and rationale against layout trials, the layout playbook section, and status.
   - Place/remove requires legal `x,y`. A ride move requires BOTH `x,y` for the
     current reachable placed ride and `new_x,new_y` from unreachable_tiles.
   - Prefer coordinates using real adjacency, water, and guest-flow evidence.
   - If no valid tile exists, the placement is impossible this turn. Do NOT retry
     the same placement. Choose another approved action or first free a tile by
     moving a low-tier ride to an unreachable tile or removing a shop.

6. PROPOSE FINAL ACTION:
   - Call `ProposeAction(action=<chosen action>, args=<approved enriched proposal
     plus required coordinates>)`.
   - ALL numeric values in args must be quoted strings. Omit price; the tool fills
     the canonical economics price.
   - If `validation.ok=FALSE`, correct the cited issue (coordinate/terrain issues
     use the layout procedure) and re-call ProposeAction.
   - After `validation.ok=TRUE`, reply with ONE sentence naming the action.

7. RECORD NEXT-TURN CONTINUITY:
   - If important next steps, observations, or a multi-turn plan must survive,
     call `scratchpad(note=<terse note>)`. Only record when required; it is deleted
     after the next read.

Preserve every procedural and reasoning step; NO shortcuts. If an action is
rejected twice or cannot execute, move to the best alternative or wait.

ERROR HANDLING: if any tool call returns an error, STOP and reply with
`ERROR: <the verbatim error text>`. Never swallow, paraphrase, retry silently,
or continue past an error.
"""
            middleware = [
                {"class": "middleware.trim_history_middleware.TrimHistoryMiddleware", "args": {}}
                {"class": "middleware.static_prompt_caching_middleware.StaticPromptCachingMiddleware", "args": {"ttl": "1h"}}
            ]
            tools = ["state_read", "ActiveTrials", "scratchpad", "FinanceGate", "ProposeAction"]
        }

        {
            name = "FinanceGate"
            class = "coded_tools.finance_gate.FinanceGate"
            function = {
                description = "Budget gate: computes daily operating cost, enriches each proposal with its derived fields, and approves or rejects it against deterministic affordability rules. An approved row carries the fully-enriched proposal."
                parameters = {
                    type = "object"
                    properties = {
                        proposals = {
                            type = "string"
                            description = "JSON-encoded array of raw domain proposals. Pass them unchanged: each needs only action/type/subtype/subclass/order_quantity/x/y/research_speed/research_topics. The gate computes one_time_cost, is_research, food/ATM and profitable-ride flags, research cost/days, and label. A tier upgrade is remove followed by place; no upgrade field exists."
                        }
                    }
                    required = ["proposals"]
                }
            }
        }

        {
            name = "ActiveTrials"
            class = "coded_tools.active_trials.ActiveTrials"
            function = {
                description = "Returns trial rules in force this episode. Omit filters to receive every domain and both macro/micro origins as joined rule and criteria records."
                parameters = {
                    type = "object"
                    properties = {
                        domain = { type = "string", description = "Optional rides/shops/staff/research/layout/survey/coordinator filter." }
                        trial_origin = { type = "string", description = "Optional micro or macro filter." }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        {
            name = "scratchpad"
            class = "coded_tools.scratchpad.Scratchpad"
            function = {
                description = "Private one-turn memo for the solo player. No args reads and clears the previous turn's note; note=<text> leaves up to 5 lines for the next turn. Writes replace; no history is kept."
                parameters = {
                    type = "object"
                    properties = { note = { type = "string", description = "Up to 5 lines for the NEXT turn only. Omit to read-and-clear." } }
                }
            }
            args = { pad = "solo_player" }
        }

        {
            name = "state_read"
            class = "coded_tools.state_read.StateRead"
            function = {
                description = "Reads one file by its operator-configured logical name. Errors if unmapped or absent. The three solo mappings replace all original playbook, economics, and status slices."
                parameters = {
                    type = "object"
                    properties = { name = { type = "string", enum = ["playbook", "economics", "status"] } }
                    required = ["name"]
                }
            }
            args = {
                max_content_chars = 120000
                name_map = {
                    playbook = ${maps_state_dir}"/playbook_all.md"
                    economics = "coded_tools/ablations/single_agent/config_files/economics_merged.md"
                    status = ${maps_state_dir}"/status_full.json"
                }
            }
        }

        {
            name = "ProposeAction"
            class = "coded_tools.propose_action.ProposeAction"
            function = {
                description = "Validates and persists ONE proposed action: action name, required fields, placement bounds, affordability, and canonical economics price. The runner reads it and steps the environment. On validation.ok=false, correct the listed reasons and call again."
                parameters = {
                    type = "object"
                    properties = {
                        action = { type = "string", enum = ["wait", "place", "move", "remove", "modify", "set_research", "survey_guests"] }
                        args = { type = "object", description = "Chosen action arguments using ActionDispatcher's layout, with every numeric value quoted as a string. Omit price; it is set from economics." }
                    }
                    required = ["action", "args"]
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}
